WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.920
Your player is digging into their own blueprint.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.680
How do you coach what you can't see?

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:10.600
This week, your player is on a parallel journey,

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.420
creating their own inner blueprint.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:16.280
This is a very vulnerable process.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:19.860
Your role as their coach is not to judge the data

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.200
that's uncovered, but to help them find meaning in it

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.600
by creating what we call psychological safety.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.880
This is the bedrock of lasting growth.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.160
It's the feeling that they can share insights

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.880
and struggles without fear of judgment.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.040
A manager I knew meant well,

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.720
but when his employees shared a past failure,

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.320
he immediately jumped in with,

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.420
well, here's what you should have done.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:48.640
He completely shut down the conversation.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.120
A Player-Coach responds differently.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.520
They might say, thank you for trusting me with that.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.400
What did that experience teach you?

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.520
The first response judges.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.360
The second invites reflection and demonstrates curiosity.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:08.660
Your playbook this week is to practice creating safety.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.920
In your next check-in, ask open-ended,

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.100
non-judgmental questions.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:18.760
Questions like, what has been the most surprising insight

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.560
from this process?

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:23.640
Now consider this, you notice your player

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.200
is only sharing positive updates.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.360
How can you gently create an opening

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:31.360
for them to discuss the challenges?

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:35.120
Go into your playbook where coaching for safety drills

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:37.900
are providing prompts to help you reinforce

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:39.920
that this is safe space for growth,

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.780
not just performance reporting.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.300
In our final segment for this lesson,

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.040
we'll build on that trust with a framework

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.560
for giving effective forward-looking feedback.
